      },
      "text": "Puerto Madryn to Gaiman"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "29dcba4d3e6d2bc058bc0da3a9e14a4e7f5dac9e8273bebfcccef65b571cf778",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-mw6m8vuu",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, head to Gaiman, one of the centres of Welsh culture in Argentina.\n\nWelsh settlers founded the town on the banks of the Chubut River in the late 19th century. On the tour, you will see the old railway station, now a local history museum, a village chapel and small historic houses with neatly kept courtyards.\n\nAfter the walk, visit Ty Te Caerdydd, a traditional tea house serving tea and cakes.\n\nThe tour ends at the Egidio Feruglio Paleontological Museum in Trelew.\n\nAn optional boat trip is available to look for Commerson’s dolphins, known locally as toninas.\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:73bcc937ffbede19",
